The unit tests do not include fail-closed test cases to verify the validator's behavior when input files are missing or malformed. Add a test case to assert that diagnostics are recorded and validation fails closed.

```javascript
  });

  test('fails closed with diagnostics when input files are missing or malformed', async () => {
    const { buildSemanticKgReviewQueue } = await import(
      '../build-semantic-kg-review-queue.mjs'
    );

    const { validatorResult } = buildSemanticKgReviewQueue({
      root: repoRoot(),
      generatedAt: '2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z',
      paths: {
        triangulationValidatorResult: 'non-existent-file.json',
        taxonomyReviewQueue: 'non-existent-file-2.json',
      },
    });

    expect(validatorResult.summary.validation_status).toBe('fail');
    expect(validatorResult.input_diagnostics.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
    expect(validatorResult.input_diagnostics[0].code).toBe('artifact_missing');
  });
});
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Include fail-closed regression test cases in unit tests for package validators to verify behavior when input files are missing or malformed, asserting that diagnostics (such as `artifact_missing`) are recorded and validation fails.
</details>

